{
  "abstract": "We prove in Lean that infinitely many primes p have Ω(p − 2) odd, where Ω counts prime factors with multiplicity, giving an affirmative answer to Green's Problem 64. The argument constructs a nonnegative weight supported on odd prime-factor parity; correlation estimates and a weighted sieve give positive total weight to integers u with u + 2 prime at arbitrarily large scales. The supporting analytic number theory is included in the formalization, with Mathlib as its only direct dependency.",
  "authors": [
